A||N||12||rider||New and looking||||1||
Z||000000||rider||11-29-2000||11:22 AM||||Hi There<BR>I've just joined the Forum and have a question. I'm looking to purchase my first Fiero, a 1986 GT, v6 4 speed, it has about 180,000 KM (about 100,000 miles) 80k on a rebuilt engine,and appears to be in good shape. I'll will be taking it out for a test on Saturday. What should I be looking for?<P>Thanks<BR>Bob<P>------------------<BR>Bob Ide<BR>rider@istar.ca<BR>bide@tcet.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||11-29-2000||12:00 PM||||Pull back the carpeting in the rear trunk over the wheelwells and check for rust.  Don't be suprised to find some rust, this is a common rust area on Fieros.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerwelcome.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||11-29-2000||12:24 PM||||Look closely at everything obviously.  If the seller is impatiant, that's just what he has to go through to sell it.<P>Check the tire wear for problems.<BR>Does it have A/C. does it work?<BR>cruise?  does it work?<BR>are the motor/tranny mounts in good shape or squishy?<BR>Any exhaust leaks?<BR>Fluid leaks? like axle seals.<BR>Does the radiator fluid look good or neglected?<BR>Does the sunroof leak? Is there rust in the slots where the sunroof tabs go?<P>OK I'll stop. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000003||rider||11-29-2000||12:27 PM||||So far so good, Thanks guys. <BR>I forgot to mention that it has a new Stainless Steel exhaust system.<P>Bob||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||11-29-2000||12:37 PM||||Check to see if everything works, including the <B>headlights</B>, even if it's daytime.  If one or both don't come open, you can complain about it and maybe drive the price down (they're not that hard to fix, really).  ||||reg||3
Z||000005||Steven||11-29-2000||01:31 PM||||Just an idea. If you are serious about the car, and you don't mind possibly throw $20 away. Offer to pay to have the oil changed. This will allow you to hear the engine without any possible engine knocking quick fixxes that the seller might be tring. And if you do buy it, you will know exactly when the oil was changed last.<p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 11-29-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||rider||11-29-2000||01:37 PM||||Great idea on the oil change, thanks.<BR>Are there any clubs in Southern Ontario/Buffalo area?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||11-29-2000||01:42 PM||||There's the <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/gtaclub/" TARGET=_blank>GTA Fiero Club</A> - Toronto||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||11-29-2000||04:49 PM||||Yes, DO get the oil changed.  My cousin worked at an oil change place, and they had a newer Blazer come in for a change.  They pulled the plug and out came out Vasaline.  It was used for getting rid of a knock, and the lady waited too long, and couldn't get her money back.  You would rather spend $20 than buy a piece of crap.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000009||killerb15||11-29-2000||09:47 PM||||Hi,The car sounds great...by the way what's he asking for it? I'm in Barrie and also looking for the exact same car!If by any chance you decide against buying the car let me know (by forum).I'm only 15, and looking to buy an 86-88 Gt for a reasonable price.<BR>Please post if you buy the car/or not, why and how much you got it for.Also if you know of any similar cars for sale I would greatly appreciate any info.<BR>    <BR>    Best of Luck-Brandon Stephens<P>P.S-Thanks for asking about a Southern Ont. Fiero club as I've been wondering if there was one too.||||reg||10
Z||000010||stimpy||11-30-2000||01:00 AM||||I'd say another good thing to look for would be play in the steering column. A lot of people are used to driving cars with power steering, and will accept some play in the wheel. In a Fiero this is more a sign of loose bolts in the column. When you move the wheel while driving, it should immeddiately respond. Good luck with your negotiations.<P>Oh, and also run a Carfax report. You can get a free one at the Carfax websie.||||reg||1
Z||000011||rider||11-30-2000||09:16 AM||||Reply to Killer.<BR>There are two cars there. The one I'm looking at is in pretty good shape and is asking $4000. The other belongs to his brother, A 85GT v6 auto, need exhaust, and some TLC. The engine runs good but the flange at the exhaust and the manifold is shot. It did recently pass the Ontario Etest so the flange thing is recent. He's asking $800 dollars Canadian but I know you can buy it for $600.||||reg||1
Z||000012||killerb15||11-30-2000||04:56 PM||||Thanks for replying, but i am really looking for an 86-88 Gt fastback if you ever come accross a "driveable"one for around $2000 post a link because i would be more than interested.<P>Thanks Anyway~Brandon ||||reg||7
